qestion 6.
change the selinux to enforsing mode

answer:
// there 2 ways to change the selinux i will show you buoth
the first: use selinux modul

- name: change selinux
  selinux:
    policy: targeted
    state: enforcing

the sec: use lineinfile modul 
// this way you can find in the exapels of lineinfile modul

- name: change selinux
  lineinfile:
    path: /etc/selinux/config
    regex: ‘^SELINUX=’
    line: ‘SELINUX=enforcing’

